From c7557e974e8e8a47234491a0936e9025971d0a95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/55] Drone tracks: a drone tone as a kit row (DroneDrum),
 with its notes as the gate and an Hz lane

A kit of drone rows is a drone track: its clips launch in Song view and sit in the arranger like any kit's, so
drones can be placed deliberately and overlap, each track with the kit's effects, volume and sidechain.

- DroneDrum (DrumType::DRONE, a NonAudioDrum like MIDI and gate rows, so their casts stay valid): a Tone and a
  Drone::Voice of its own. Its notes open its gate through its arpeggiator as a gate row's do (with the arp on, it
  gates the tone in rhythm); the tone fades in and out as the song's drone's tones do. allowNoteTails and
  hasAnyVoices (the gate) as for gate rows: a note as long as the clip holds across the loop point.
- Its pitch: the tone's own, with the row's Hz lane on top: the NoteRow's expression X (pitch bend), in cents
  (DroneTrackPitch). So an empty lane changes nothing, and saving (expressionData), cloning, recording to the
  arranger and undo work as for any automation. It plays through ExpressionParamSet ->
  polyphonicExpressionEventOnChannelOrNote(); noteOn() takes the lane's full 32 bits where the note starts. Between
  nodes it steps (expression isn't interpolated) and the voice glides there in about 15 ms.
- changePitch(): with REC on, the clock running and the clip armed, the new pitch goes into the lane at the play
  position as a gold knob records (AutoParam::setCurrentValueInResponseToUserInput(): a node, latched until the next
  turn; into the clone while recording to the arranger). Otherwise the tone's own frequency changes, which moves the
  lane with it.
- Kit::renderGlobalEffectableForClip() walks the kit's drums and renders the sounding drone rows into the kit's
  buffer (not drumsWithRenderingActive, which is for SoundDrums: that caused the E253/E321 freezes). The block's
  context once per kit and block, only when a drone row sounds.
- Level: a row in a new kit (volume 3/4 up) sounds as loud as a tone of the song's drone at the same level with the
  drone's volume at its default (40): measured in the emulator, the kit's stages put it 6.71 dB lower, kGain makes up
  for it.
- NoteRow::clearMPEUpUntilNextNote() leaves a drone row's lane alone: adding or deleting a note would otherwise
  erase it.
- File: <droneTone mode timbre byNote note cents frequency beat sync triplet pulseAttack pulseRelease level pan>
  (the song's drone's tone attributes), its arpeggiator and, in songs, MIDI commands; Kit::readFromFile() and
  StorageManager::createNewDrum() know it. The lane stays in the song's noteRow. Older firmware skips the tag, so the
  kit's later rows shift.
- The drone's tone menu edits a drone row's tone when drone::trackTone points at it (set by the clip view's menu,
  next commit); a deleted row clears it.

